From: Aspartame GTK4 migration
Subject: [PATCH] controlpanel: use the complete monitor geometry

The GTK4 Control Panel already owns the Settings surface, but its geometry
was deliberately reduced by two Sugar grid cells.  That leaves the Home
toolbar and white margins visible around the modal panel.  Request the full
monitor dimensions; Activity surfaces and the shell remain separate.

--- a/src/jarabe/controlpanel/gui.py
+++ b/src/jarabe/controlpanel/gui.py
@@ -183,3 +183,3 @@ class ControlPanel(Gtk.Window):
         offset = style.GRID_CELL_SIZE
-        width = sw - offset * 2
-        height = sh - offset * 2
+        width = sw
+        height = sh
